    "summaryAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are r",
    "descriptionAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. Co-create the future with us as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software. * Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab. Commercial Account Executive, Mid-Market, Belgium &amp; Luxembourg Remote | Hiring in the Netherlands or France GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. More than 50 million registered users, and more than half of the Fortune 100, trust us to ship better, more secure software faster. We’re all-remote, with a public handbook, a high-performance culture and a values-led way of working. This is a place where careers accelerate, and where you’ll work with sharp people who care about customers and getting things done. An overview of this role Belgium and Luxembourg are a great market for GitLab: a dense mix of fast-growing, engineering-led mid-sized companies, all modernizing how they plan, build, secure and ship software. As Mid-Market AE, you’ll own the territory end to end, from first conversation to close to long-term adoption. You’ll work alongside Sales Development, Solutions Architects, Customer Success, Renewals and Partners. Together you’ll use value-based selling (MEDDPICC and Command of the Message) to build pipeline, forecast accurately and grow GitLab’s footprint. Location and language Covers Belgium and Luxembourg, but you must be based in the Netherlands or France. We can’t hire for this role in Belgium itself. Fluent Dutch and English, or French and English. Regular travel within the territory to meet customers and attend events. What you’ll do Own the Mid-Market book of business in Belgium and Luxembourg, new and expansion, as the CEO of your territory. Build pipeline through consistent prospecting and run disciplined, well-documented sales cycles. Show customers the value of GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform to both business and technical teams. Partner with Sales Development, Solutions Architects, Customer Success, Renewals and our Partner ecosystem to win and grow accounts. Drive adoption, prevent churn and forecast accurately against your quota. Host and attend regional events to build relationships with customers and prospects. Share win/loss learnings, improve our sales handbook, and be the voice of the customer in our public issue tracker. What you’ll bring DevOps, DevSecOps, Security, Software or SaaS sales experience, with a track record of value-based selling to business and technical stakeholders. Fluency in Dutch and English, or French and English. Strong discovery, negotiation and closing skills, plus comfort with outbound prospecting. A genuine desire to see customers succeed with GitLab, and an interest in open source and developer tooling (Git, DevOps or ALM experience is a bonus). Willingness to travel to meet customers in person. Alignment with GitLab’s values: Collaboration, Results for Customers, Efficiency, Diversity, Inclusion &amp; Belonging, Iteration, and Transparency. About the team You’ll join GitLab’s Sales organization as part of a distributed team of Account Executives, Sales Development, Solutions Architects, Renewals and Partner colleagues. We work asynchronously and share playbooks and best practices in the handbook. You’ll get structure and support, and the autonomy to run your territory your way. How GitLab supports you Competitive on-target earnings with uncapped incentive pay Equity and Employee Stock Purchase Plan Flexible paid time off Growth and Development Fund Parental leave Team Member Resource Groups True all-remote working, wherever you’re most fulfilled Many successful candidates don’t meet every requirement on paper. If you’re excited about this role, apply and let our recruiters take a look. How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being Flexible Paid Time Off&nbsp; Team Member Resource Groups Equity Compensation &amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan Growth and Development Fund Parental Leave &nbsp; Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from underrepresented groups are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you're excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application. Country Hiring Guidelines: GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&nbsp;&nbsp; Privacy Policy: Please review our Recruitment Privacy Policy. Your privacy is important to us. GitLab is pr",
