    "summaryAr": "About this Team The HR Business Partner (HRBP) team at OpenAI partners with leaders on complex organizational and talent decisions where the right path is not always obvious. We stay close enough to the business to understand how it works and focus our time on the decisions that benefit most from our judgment, context, and influence. We work with urgency, empathy, and sound judgment. We value sincerity, intellectual ",
    "descriptionAr": "About this Team The HR Business Partner (HRBP) team at OpenAI partners with leaders on complex organizational and talent decisions where the right path is not always obvious. We stay close enough to the business to understand how it works and focus our time on the decisions that benefit most from our judgment, context, and influence. We work with urgency, empathy, and sound judgment. We value sincerity, intellectual honesty, and collaboration over ego. About this Role As a Senior HR Business Partner supporting Tech, you’ll partner with leaders in engineering, product, and other technical teams as they build and scale their organizations. You’ll get close enough to the work to understand what’s slowing teams down, then help leaders make decisions about structure, talent, and how teams work together as technical priorities evolve. This is an individual contributor role reporting to an HRBP Lead. You’ll advise senior leaders on complex decisions and work directly with managers to make those decisions stick. In this role, you will: Translate technical priorities into org and talent decisions. Help leaders decide what capabilities to build, how to structure teams, and where ownership needs to sit. Diagnose what’s getting in the way of team performance. Use data and input from the people doing the work to separate structural issues from problems with roles, priorities, or how teams work together. Develop technical leaders. Coach managers through performance, growth, and succession decisions, and help them set clear expectations for both people managers and individual contributors. Lead change as technical priorities shift. Help leaders think through the impact of reorganizations or changes in ownership and communicate decisions clearly to the teams affected. Build People practices that work for technical teams. Partner with fellow HRBPs and People specialists to adapt performance, development, and talent processes without adding unnecessary overhead. You might thrive in this role if you have: 7–10+ years of HR experience, including at least 5 years as an HR Business Partner in a high-growth or complex environment. Experience partnering with engineering, product, or other technical organizations, and curiosity about how technical teams make decisions and deliver work. A track record of helping technical leaders navigate org design, workforce planning, or talent decisions as teams grow or priorities change. Skill in coaching senior leaders and managers, including the ability to challenge a decision constructively and maintain trust. Sound judgment under pressure and the ability to act on incomplete information while staying open to new evidence. Discretion, fairness, and sound judgment when the stakes are high. Workplace & Location This role is based in our San Francisco or New York office and is not available remotely. We offer relocation support to new employees. Our hybrid model is three days in the office per week, with optional work from home on Thursdays and Fridays. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
