    "summaryAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look f",
    "descriptionAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look for slope over intercept. We care less about where you trained and more about what you’ve built. At Ramp, everyone is a builder who owns problems end to end and makes consequential decisions that shape the outcome. The median Ramp customer saves 7.5% and grows revenue 16% in their first year – far in excess of businesses operating without Ramp. We believe every ambitious company deserves the same. If you want to build systems that directly shape how companies move and manage billions, Ramp is the place to do it. About the Role Homepage is the most visited surface in Ramp. It is where finance teams and employees land each day to see what needs their attention, from approvals and receipts to account setup and recommendations. Behind it sits a shared platform that brings work from teams across Ramp into one ranked, actionable feed. Ramp's Product Foundations team builds shared product capabilities across Ramp’s product surfaces. Our goal is platforms that are so well defined and dependable that product teams can self-serve on them, while customers get a fast, focused, and consistent experience. We're looking for a senior backend engineer to own a core part of that foundation. You'll take responsibility for an area such as Homepage performance and reliability, set its technical direction within the team, and keep it fast and correct as more teams and task types build on it. You'll work closely with frontend, product, design, and engineering partners across Ramp to raise the bar on quality, speed, and adoption. What You'll Do Own the design and evolution of a core part of Ramp's Homepage backend, from technical design through launch, monitoring, and iteration Improve our product platforms, with a focus on latency, reliability, and graceful behavior at scale Build shared frameworks, such as standard task actions and detail views, so every team's tasks behave consistently and get new capabilities for free Evolve how key areas like Homepage surface work, including running and evaluating experiments that improve task completion and relevance Extend the platform to support new items and suggestions relevant to users Make the platform simple and safe for other Ramp engineers to adopt, with clear abstractions, strong defaults, documentation, and good developer tooling Drive technical direction for your area, connect long-term system health to the team's roadmap, and raise the engineering bar through design reviews, code reviews, and mentorship Share ownership of platform reliability with the team, including on-call and incident follow-up What You'll Need Experience designing, building, and operating production backend systems, including APIs, data models, and asynchronous or event-driven workflows A track record of owning a system or product area end to end and shaping its technical direction over time Strong system design judgment, especially around performance, reliability, and correctness for high-traffic services Experience building platforms, shared services, or abstractions that other engineers depend on Product sense: you care about the experience of the people using what you build, and you balance speed with quality Clear written and verbal communication, and comfort aligning engineers, product, and design across teams while working remotely Nice to Haves Experience with ranking, recommendations, or feed systems, including experimentation and measuring their impact Experience diagnosing and improving latency in high-traffic product surfaces Experience building task, workflow, notification, or collaboration platforms Benefits available to all full-time Ramp employees (Global) Flexible PTO Centralized home-office equipment ordering Health and wellness stipend Budget for intra-office travel Weekly coffee stipend United States 100% medical, dental & vision insurance coverage for you, with partial coverage for dependents One Medical annual membership 401(k), including employer match on contributions made while employed by Ramp Fertility HRA (up to $10,000 per year) Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay Pet insurance In-office perks: lunch, snacks, drinks, and more Relocation expense coverage to NYC or SF (if needed) Canada Group medical, dental, and vision coverage through Sun Life Life, AD&D, and disability coverage Fertility drug coverage (up to $4,000 lifetime) Group Retirement Plan with employer match (RRSP + DPSP) Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay, with additional time available at reduced pay Employee Assistance Program and virtual care through Lumino Health United Kingdom Private medical insurance through Freedom Elite Virtual GP and at-home care via eMed x Livi Workplace pension through Penfold, with salary sacrifice option Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay with additional time available at reduced pay Referral Instructions If you are being referred for the role, please contact that person to apply on your behalf. Other notices Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. Beware of recruiting scams: Ramp will only contact you through official @ Ramp.com email addresses and will never ask for payment or sensitive personal information during the hiring process. Ramp Applicant Privacy Notice",
