    "summaryAr": "About the team The Global Ad Solutions team helps businesses connect with people in useful, relevant ways through OpenAI’s advertising products. We partner with advertisers and agencies to understand their goals, build effective strategies, and demonstrate the value of our platform, while putting the user experience and trust at the center of everything we do. We are building an advertising business from the ground u",
    "descriptionAr": "About the team The Global Ad Solutions team helps businesses connect with people in useful, relevant ways through OpenAI’s advertising products. We partner with advertisers and agencies to understand their goals, build effective strategies, and demonstrate the value of our platform, while putting the user experience and trust at the center of everything we do. We are building an advertising business from the ground up. That means working across Sales, Product, Marketing, Measurement and Operations to solve new problems, shape how we go to market, and help our customers grow alongside us. About the role We’re looking for a Sales Manager to build, lead and develop a high-performing team of Client Partners and Customer Success Managers serving advertisers in regulated industries such as financial services (including insurance) and healthcare and life sciences. You’ll own your team’s revenue performance, customer relationships and execution, while helping define the sales practices and culture that will enable our business to scale. You are a hands-on leader who can coach through a complex customer conversation, build an actionable plan from data, and bring clarity and focus in a fast-changing environment. You balance near-term results with long-term customer partnerships and make thoughtful decisions that protect user trust. You’ll help the team build durable partnerships with advertisers whose campaigns require close coordination across marketing, legal and compliance. You’ll coach the team to identify where OpenAI’s advertising products can meet customer goals, set clear expectations early and protect user trust as the business grows. In this role, you will: Hire, coach and develop a diverse team of Client Partners and Customer Success Managers, providing clear expectations, regular feedback and opportunities for growth. Own the team’s revenue and business objectives, building account plans and pipeline around opportunities that fit advertiser goals and platform policies. Establish a consistent operating rhythm for account reviews, forecasting and prioritization, using data to identify risks, opportunities and actions. Coach Client Partners and Customer Success Managers on executive relationships, complex negotiations and business cases that account for advertiser approval processes, policy requirements and measurement needs. Build senior relationships with key advertisers and agencies, serving as an executive partner and escalation point when needed. Partner closely with Agency, Marketing Science, Solutions Engineering, Product, Legal and Policy to address questions early and give advertisers clear guidance on campaign requirements and measurement. Bring customer and market insights back to internal teams, helping shape product priorities, sales strategy and go-to-market execution. Develop repeatable tools, processes and best practices that improve how the team works as the business grows. Foster a culture of ownership, collaboration, candor and continuous learning, while upholding OpenAI’s commitment to user trust and responsible growth. You might thrive in this role if you: Have 10+ years of experience in digital advertising, media, marketing solutions or a related client-facing commercial role, including 3+ years leading and developing sales teams. Have a track record of building or growing teams and delivering against ambitious revenue goals in a dynamic environment. Have experience advising senior advertisers or agency stakeholders in one or more regulated industries and navigating commercial decisions involving marketing, legal and compliance teams. Understand how regulated advertisers evaluate brand and performance campaigns and how approval processes, privacy requirements and platform policies can shape campaign design and measurement. Understand both brand and performance advertising, including how advertisers use measurement and business outcomes to evaluate investment. Use data to prioritize opportunities, inspect a pipeline, improve forecast quality and turn insights into clear action. Can work across functions to solve customer problems and translate recurring feedback into scalable improvements. Are comfortable building through ambiguity, moving with urgency, and adapting your approach as the business evolves. Communicate clearly and credibly with a range of audiences, from individual contributors to executives, and care deeply about earning customer and user trust. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: pro",
