    "summaryAr": "About the Team OpenAI’s Legal team plays a crucial role in advancing our mission by tackling innovative and fundamental legal issues in AI. The team includes professionals from diverse legal fields—technology, AI, infrastructure, privacy, IP, corporate, employment, tax, regulatory, and litigation—who collaborate closely with colleagues across the company. If you are passionate about being a technology lawyer working ",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team OpenAI’s Legal team plays a crucial role in advancing our mission by tackling innovative and fundamental legal issues in AI. The team includes professionals from diverse legal fields—technology, AI, infrastructure, privacy, IP, corporate, employment, tax, regulatory, and litigation—who collaborate closely with colleagues across the company. If you are passionate about being a technology lawyer working on cutting-edge challenges, you’ll thrive here. About the Role We’re seeking a senior lawyer to participate in commercial legal strategy and execution across OpenAI’s fast-growing data center portfolio, with an emphasis on leasing and colocation. In this cross-functional role, you’ll partner closely with infrastructure, procurement, supply chain, partnerships, and finance teams to structure, negotiate, and manage the transactions that support OpenAI’s data center projects. We’re looking for an experienced infrastructure or real estate transactions lawyer who thrives in ambiguity and wants to help define the commercial playbook for OpenAI’s data center operations and securing, building, and expanding data center capacity. This role reports to the Associate General Counsel for Infrastructure. We use a hybrid work model of 3-days in the office per week and offer relocation assistance to new employees. In this role, you will: Own commercial legal strategy and risk management for OpenAI’s data center projects, from site selection through delivery, operations, and expansion, and financing of those projects. Draft, negotiate, and advise on powered-shell and build-to-suit leases and services agreements, work letters, master colocation agreements, and site-specific service orders on behalf of OpenAI as tenant or customer. Work with engineering and operations teams to negotiate power and cooling commitments, commissioning and acceptance criteria, service levels, and remedies for delayed delivery or outages. Support strategic partnerships involving AI infrastructure and hardware supply chains for data center builds and expansions. Develop frameworks for procurement, licensing, and collaboration with the developers, operators, and suppliers supporting OpenAI’s data centers. Partner with finance and operations teams to align contract terms with business and compliance requirements, including when rent or service fees begin and how power costs are allocated. Collaborate with policy and regulatory colleagues and local counsel on data center site diligence, including zoning, permitting, and utility access. Build scalable, efficient contracting processes that support OpenAI’s data center development at speed while managing risk. You might thrive in this role if you: Bring 8+ years of legal experience, with a substantial focus on technology transactions and commercial contracting. Have a JD and a license or qualification to practice in CA or the state in which you are based, or the right to practice in such location. Have hands-on experience independently drafting and negotiating data center leases and colocation agreements, including technical exhibits governing capacity, delivery, and operations. Have experience advising on real estate matters for data center projects, including site control, title and survey review, and easements for power, fiber, and access. Demonstrate the ability to operate with autonomy and sound judgment in highly technical and fast-moving environments. Bring exceptional communication skills and an ability to distill complexity into actionable, business-aligned guidance. Have experience advising on cross-border deals. Have prior experience with infrastructure supply agreements, joint ventures, or other complex commercial deals supporting data center construction or operations is a strong plus. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to",
